{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974729-complications-and-consolations","id":974729,"title":"Complications and Consolations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-22T16:25:52-07:00","id":974729,"title":"Complications and Consolations","content":"Anyone else really, really hate this mechanic? It's really just the one part I have a problem with, where the player chooses if it's a success with a complication or if it's a failure with a consolation.<br /> <br /> I mean, players are always going to choose the success right? Even if it's a super high difficulty. This could wildly disrupt a story. If the players try to convince the villain to just stop doing what he's doing, as long as one of them gets one success, then the bad guy has to go along with it, even if there's a massive complication involved. I guess you could just make the roll impossible, then you miss out on having them actually having a chance of accomplishing something.<br /> <br /> Moreover, what if you, as the GM, have a really good idea for a good consolation, but then the players opt for a complication instead, so you have to whip up something not nearly as good. &quot;Uh... your foot is sore now.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know other systems like 13th Age use a similar mechanic, but I've never seen them in action. I'll probably end up changing it to GM's choice in my games, but I am curious if I'm the only one who has a problem with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:05:59-07:00","id":974758,"title":"","content":"I'm a diehard storygame guy, so the whole 'failing forward' thing is totally fine by me. Any players I'd game with I trust to care enough about drama to not always go for the optimized choice in the name of the greater narrative.<br /> <br /> There's also common sense to factor in. If your game has &quot;convince the villain to stop the plot&quot; as a single roll of the dice, that's a failure on the Storyguide's side of the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:12:00-07:00","id":974765,"title":"","content":"I am weary of the system a little bit but it does state that if u do not atleast succeed in the base difficulty then you can not choose a complication. It gives the example of if you cant even get a single success than you can't do a succeed but situation. It seems like the basic difficulty would be much higher for a task like that. If you randomly throw out a difficulty of 7 for example then im sure the basic success would atleast 5 successes. Its like &quot;close, but not quite&quot;. Also, it states that if something is deemed impossible by the ST than you simply shouldnt even roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:50:32-07:00","id":974784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974729-complications-and-consolations?p=974758#post974758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's also common sense to factor in. If your game has &quot;convince the villain to stop the plot&quot; as a single roll of the dice, that's a failure on the Storyguide's side of the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but it limits your options as a storyteller significantly. You can either A) Not allow them to interact with a villain (lame) B) Make it impossible for them to convince the Villain to give up his grandiose scheme at all (lame) or C) Allow them to make the roll and if they roll at least one success, they succeed (with a complication), or D) Have it be multiple rolls, all of which can be succeeded on a complication.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:21:12-07:00","id":974794,"title":"","content":"If the rolls not super important, or I think it's just as interesting to fail, I'd take Consolation over Complication. Sometimes just whiffing a hit and gaining +1 Momentum is better than losing your weapon, especially if you can build that Momentum up for a big hit later.<br /> <br /> The big thing about this part of the system IMO is that the SG and the players need to be working together to make a better story. If the SG can't think of a good Complication, the player should probably just let it go and take a point of Momentum. The rules say that in the Note to Storyguides.<br /> <br /> Also, if the SG doesn't think success or failure (with or without complications) on a roll would fun or interesting, then no roll should be called for at all. It should just not be possible, or automatically happen. The rules basically say that right at the beginning of the Rolling in Scion section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 09-22-2016, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:21:53-07:00","id":974795,"title":"","content":"Well, to reiterate:<br /> <br /> A Note to Storyguides<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t have to create Complications on the fly to help your players\u2019 characters. The system is meant to fine-tune what fate they suffer when the dice don\u2019t go their way - success with a negative, or failure with a positive. Just declare Difficulties up-front based on total circumstances. If things get wonky, feel free to toss the players Momentum and call it a day.<br /> <br /> Same goes for if it gets tiresome. C&amp;C are meant to be flexible tools in your toolbox that other things in the system key off of - not a straightjacket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}